// Far shadow cascade reuse (PERF_TODO F3): the cached far map must never pop. Run from OpenGLTest/:
//   VOXEL_TIME=400 VOXEL_DEBUG=1 VOXEL_SCRIPT=visual-examples/far-shadow.json
// VOXEL_TIME 400 puts the shots at a lighting clock of about 430, a sun about 5 degrees up, whose
// long shadows reach the far cascade (ShadowCascade, FarShadowReuse). The eye hovers 30 blocks over
// lod-horizon.json's summit A looking +Z, across the sun (which sets toward -X), so terrain 300-450
// blocks out, where the far fade band lies, fills the upper half of the frame.
// Part 1 (still_*): twelve shots 0.1 s apart at one pose; they straddle the re-renders a still
// camera gets (the max age and the key light turning half a texel), which must show no step.
// Part 2 (step_*): forty teleports 4 blocks along the view, a shot after each; the look-following
// far center re-centers at least once on the way, which must not move the far fade band visibly.
// Compare consecutive shots pairwise (mean absolute difference) against the same pairs captured
// on a build without the reuse.
